{{if:table:before_after}}The first version of this study measured production code at `2a8e47735`
(backup branch `{{ba.ref|s}}`). The table compares the main admission dynamics of the
demand sweep (§6.2) with the new code; the old values are read from the generated
values committed on the backup branch, the new ones from this run. Both use the same
workload, seeds and analysis.

{{table:before_after}}

The harness's client model also changed with the production client (§5.3): an
advertiser that abandons now stays away from the registrar for one ad lifetime
(Registration's overloaded set), late retries are credited with the scheduled wait,
and sub-floor quotes are raised to 1 s. The differences therefore combine registrar
changes (G term, expiry on access, lower-bound changes #166/#177) and client changes;
they are not attributed to individual pull requests.
{{else}}*Provisional: no comparison was generated (missing old values or new demand sweep).*{{endif}}
